Resolve the supplied Cues that are not yet represented by accepted object pages. Use read, write and edit, with no outside knowledge. Their full source title, section, Cue and details are supplied in the user prompt. Every catalog page has status context_only: existing object and concept pages are read-only context, and this stage has no consumable page members. Read relevant indexes and bodies to determine scope and existing coverage.

For each supplied Cue, either adopt its supported detail into a written object draft or record a supported final non-adoption reason. A source can be a method, model, dataset, benchmark, concrete research work or other independently identifiable object. Abstract material alone is not a reason to discard a Cue; consider whether it describes an identifiable method or work. Preserve meaningful object and version boundaries, conditions and source attribution. A Cue need not describe an independent object by itself: mechanisms, component details, evaluation protocols/results, design purposes, limitations, licensing and reproducibility records belong in the draft for their identified object or concrete research work. Do not discard those details merely because another Cue names the object, or because an existing concept already discusses them. Group all related supplied Cues into a coherent object draft for subsequent merging. Do not invent a named implementation or label a generic explanation as an object.

Every ref in required_object_adoption_refs must appear as an inline citation supporting substantive detail in an output object draft. These Cues have nonempty historical_concept_refs: the listed P pages already use them as conceptual evidence, so their evidence must be represented in the object layer. Read those historical pages to identify the corresponding object or concrete research work, then write the supported detail into a draft. Coverage in a read-only historical page does not complete this assignment. These Cues cannot be deferred or discarded.

Write drafts to pages/O1.md, pages/O2.md, etc., with exactly title and description frontmatter, substantive H2 sections and inline [[N#]] citations. Each draft must adopt at least one supplied unplaced Cue. Do not add URLs, Markdown links, HTML, H1, other frontmatter, Related or Evidence sections. User-facing text follows output_language. Refer to proper object names, not local P/S/N references in prose.

Write result.json with exactly the fields shown in this all-adopted example: {"pages":[{"file":"pages/O1.md","member_refs":[]}],"retained_refs":[],"discarded_refs":[],"deferred_entries":[]}. List each written draft once. Every pages[].member_refs is [], and retained_refs and discarded_refs are []; N refs identify Cues, not page members, and no P page can be consumed here.

Adoption is recorded only by inline [[N#]] citations in the written Markdown drafts. The manifest is not a per-Cue completion log. deferred_entries contains only supplied Cues that appear in no output draft and have a specific source-supported reason for final non-adoption, using {"entry_ref":"the supplied Cue ref","reason":"the supported final non-adoption reason"}. Never put a cited Cue in deferred_entries, and never use an adoption statement such as "included in the draft" as a deferral reason. If all supplied Cues are adopted, deferred_entries is [].

Before stopping, inspect the written drafts and manifest together: every supplied Cue is either cited in a draft or deferred with a supported reason, never both; every required_object_adoption_refs Cue is cited; every page member array is empty. Source-backed drafts will enter global target planning, where duplicate identities can be merged with existing objects. Inputs under /work/wiki are read-only; only write under /work. Runtime returns exact validation feedback to this same session, at most three total submissions including the initial submission. On rejection, repair all reported violations and repeat this complete disposition check while preserving valid content. Stop after writing the files.
